<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Time</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>time
</pre>
<p>Tells you the time in the world: the hour, the day of the week, and the 
date, for example:
</p>
<pre>It is 3 PM, on the Day of the Moon,
   the 5th Day of the Month of the Sun, Year 281.
</pre>
<p>Time in Valhalla runs twelve times faster than real time. An hour lasts 
five minutes, a day two hours, and a month of fourteen days 28 hours. A 
year has nine months and passes in 252 hours, ten and a half real days, so 
some 35 years go by in a real year. Your character ages with it (see 
<a cmd='#'>Help Age</a>).
</p><p>The seven days of the week are the Days of the Moon, the Bull, the 
Deception, Thunder, Freedom, the Great Gods and the Sun. The nine months 
run from winter to the dark of autumn: the Months of Winter, the Winter 
Wolf, the Frost Giant, Spring, Futility, the Sun, the Heat, the Long 
Shadows and the Ancient Darkness.
</p><p>The time matters: shops keep hours, some city gates are locked at night, 
and the light changes with the hour (see <a cmd='#'>Help Weather</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Weather</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Age</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Score</a>
</pre>




</div>